CAT = "saLicence"; SEG = "LIC"
# Traffic Law (Royal Decree M/85 of 1428H, as amended). Articles checked in the Arabic text.
Q = [
("Under the Traffic Law, who may drive a car on a public road in Saudi Arabia?",
 "Holders of a valid licence", ["Anyone aged 18 or over", "Anyone with car insurance", "Anyone the owner allows"],
 "No one may drive any vehicle before getting the licence the Traffic Law and its regulation require for that vehicle. Age, insurance or the owner's permission do not replace it."),
("Which document must stay inside the vehicle whenever it is being driven?",
 "Vehicle registration", ["Purchase contract", "Last service record", "Customs clearance papers"],
 "The Traffic Law says the vehicle's registration (rukhsat sayr) must be in the vehicle while it is on the move, and a security officer may ask to see it."),
("A security officer asks for your driving licence at a checkpoint. What may the officer do with it?",
 "Inspect it only", ["Keep it until you pay", "Keep it for a week", "Pass it to the court"],
 "The law gives the officer the right to ask for and inspect a licence or registration, but not to hold on to it."),
("A shop owner asks to keep your driving licence as security for a rental. What does the Traffic Law say?",
 "Forbids holding it", ["Allows it as a deposit", "Allows it if you agree in writing", "Leaves it to the shop"],
 "Holding a driving licence or a vehicle registration with another person, or pledging it, is forbidden by the Traffic Law."),
("What does the Traffic Law require every driver to have for the vehicle?",
 "Insurance cover", ["Dash camera fitted", "Tracking device", "Spare roof light"],
 "The amended Traffic Law obliges every driver to insure the vehicle; driving without an insurance document is a violation."),
("How does the Traffic Law check that vehicles stay fit to use on the road?",
 "Periodic inspection", ["Checks after a crash", "Owner's yearly check", "Inspection on resale"],
 "All vehicles of every type are subject to periodic technical inspection at approved centres, and skipping it is a violation."),
("How many number plates must a private car carry?",
 "Two: one front, one rear", ["One, at the rear only", "One, at the front only", "Two, both at the rear"],
 "Every vehicle except a motorcycle, trailer or semi-trailer carries two visible, readable plates, one at the front and one at the rear."),
("You want to change your car's colour. What does the Traffic Law require?",
 "Authority's prior permission", ["Notice within a week after", "Inspection at the next renewal", "Workshop's paint certificate"],
 "Changing a vehicle's colour, features, basic equipment, load or dimensions is forbidden without prior permission, and workshops may not do it without a permit either."),
("A friend offers to fit flashing lights like an emergency vehicle's to your car. This is:",
 "Not allowed unless authorised", ["Allowed if amber, not red", "Allowed if kept switched off", "Banned for all vehicles"],
 "Fitting or using unauthorised sound or light warning devices is forbidden, and equipment like that of official or emergency vehicles is a violation."),
("An owner lets a person with no licence drive the car, and a crash follows. The owner:",
 "Shares liability for damage", ["Bears all liability alone", "Has no liability at all", "Liable only if in the car"],
 "An owner or person in charge who lets an unlicensed person drive is penalised and, if a crash results, shares the financial liability as the court decides."),
("Under the amended Traffic Law, when may an owner let someone else drive the vehicle?",
 "With an authorisation (tafweed)", ["With a notarised letter only", "With a written insurance note", "With the owner in the car"],
 "The amended article says an owner may not let another person drive the vehicle except under an authorisation (tafweed) issued through the set procedure."),
("You arrive with a valid licence recognised by the traffic authority. For how long may you use it?",
 "One year, or to its expiry", ["Three months, or to its expiry", "Two years, or to its expiry", "Six months, or to its expiry"],
 "A recognised international or foreign licence may be used for one year from entry into the Kingdom, or until it expires if that comes first."),
("What happens when a driver's violation points pass the allowed maximum?",
 "Licence withdrawn for a period", ["Fine doubled for a period", "Retraining course required", "Car impounded for a period"],
 "Each violation carries points by how much it endangers safety; once the record passes the maximum, the licence is withdrawn for a set period."),
("A load falls from an overloaded vehicle and injures someone. Who is held responsible?",
 "Its driver", ["Only the vehicle's owner", "Only the loading firm", "No one, as an accident"],
 "The driver is responsible for harm caused by loads over the legal weights and dimensions or by unsafe loading, unless another person's liability is proven."),
("You must tow a broken-down car at night. What does the Traffic Law require on the towed car?",
 "Side and rear reflectors", ["Hazard lights on the tow car", "Someone walking behind it", "Tow rope of 10 m or more"],
 "A trailer or a broken-down vehicle being towed must have rear and side lights or reflectors so others can see it."),
("A licence holder develops a condition that makes driving unsafe. The traffic authority may:",
 "Cancel it or refuse renewal", ["Suspend it or add limits", "Fine the holder or warn them", "Order a retest or a course"],
 "The authority may cancel a licence, or refuse to renew it, once it is shown the holder has lost the medical fitness to drive."),
("Your driving licence has expired but you feel fine to drive. Driving now is:",
 "Not allowed until renewed", ["Allowed for 60 days more", "Allowed only in your city", "Not allowed after one year"],
 "Driving with a licence whose validity has ended is listed as a violation in the Traffic Law's violation tables. Renew it before you drive."),
("What does the Traffic Law require of your number plates?",
 "Readable and uncovered", ["Tinted to cut sun glare", "Removed while parked", "Any style the owner likes"],
 "Plates must be visible and readable, only plates issued by the authority may be used, and hiding or blurring a vehicle's identifying features is a violation."),
("A person with a physical disability wants a driving licence. What does the law require?",
 "Approved medical report", ["Adapted-car certificate", "Doctor's note from any clinic", "Family member's consent"],
 "People with special needs may get a licence after an approved medical report shows they can drive, under rules set in the regulation."),
("You sold your car but the ownership transfer is not finished. Who is still liable for its fees?",
 "Registered owner", ["New buyer only", "Car dealer", "Insurance company"],
 "The registered owner stays responsible for fees and obligations on the vehicle until the transfer is done, and can claim back from the new owner."),
]
